us of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(4,-1),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{25} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533942 true] [17592186267556 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267557 13194139533942 true] [17592186267556 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267558 13194139533942 true] [17592186267556 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533942 true] [17592186267556 1041 "field-1" 13194139533942 true] [17592186267556 1104 #edb/ref 17592186267557 13194139533942 true] [17592186267556 1110 #uuid "86eeb558-0a17-5eec-92c7-1bda3882a012" 13194139533942 true] [17592186267557 1034 "\\frac{(x-4)^2}{4}+\\frac{(y+1)^2}{25}" 13194139533942 true] [17592186267557 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533942 true] [17592186267557 1111 #uuid "fe076377-8319-5645-a6ba-da20eaf3197e" 13194139533942 true] [17592186267558 1034 "\\frac{(x-4)^2}{25}+\\frac{(y+1)^2}{4}" 13194139533942 true] [17592186267558 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533942 true] [17592186267558 1111 #uuid "77f37205-cdd0-5c13-b381-5ff81058df31" 13194139533942 true] [17592186267559 1017 #edb/ref 17592186267560 13194139533942 true] [17592186267559 1017 #edb/ref 17592186267562 13194139533942 true] [17592186267559 1089 "q-278402" 13194139533942 true] [17592186267559 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533942 true] [17592186267559 1100 "For the ellipse $\\frac{(x+7)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{11}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." 13194139533942 true] [17592186267559 1113 #uuid "b74a983b-5b3e-5c81-aeef-49a17e380aae" 13194139533942 true] [17592186267559 1145 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=-7$ and $k=-5,$ so the center is located at $(-7,-5).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=3$ and ${b}^{2}=11.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=3,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=11,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{11}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=\\sqrt{11},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{11}=2\\sqrt{11},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{3}=2\\sqrt{3}.$" 13194139533942 true] [17592186267560 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267561 13194139533942 true] [17592186267560 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533942 true] [17592186267560 1041 "field-1" 13194139533942 true] [17592186267560 1104 #edb/ref 17592186267561 13194139533942 true] [17592186267560 1110 #uuid "c0a3e32c-7502-5d12-a165-e06a2e52dcdd" 13194139533942 true] [17592186267561 1034 "2\\sqrt{11}" 13194139533942 true] [17592186267561 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533942 true] [17592186267561 1111 #uuid "97a56b89-7939-55e5-aa7f-0de277930e6d" 13194139533942 true] [17592186267562 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267563 13194139533942 true] [17592186267562 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533942 true] [17592186267562 1041 "field-2" 13194139533942 true] [17592186267562 1104 #edb/ref 17592186267563 13194139533942 true] [17592186267562 1110 #uuid "8d3002bc-bbe1-5c58-b61e-5c7eeded7b0d" 13194139533942 true] [17592186267563 1034 "2\\sqrt{3}" 13194139533942 true] [17592186267563 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533942 true] [17592186267563 1111 #uuid "375397a9-b308-5964-af77-9cc319b096b3" 13194139533942 true] [17592186267564 1017 #edb/ref 1759